According to a report by IntelMarketResearch, the global Assisted Reproductive Technology Market was valued at USD 45.08 billion in 2025 and is expected to reach USD 61.2 billion by 2034, growing at a CAGR of 3.03% over the forecast period. Assisted Reproductive Technology includes clinical procedures involving the manipulation of oocytes and embryos to address infertility, including in-vitro fertilization, fertility medication, hormonal stimulation and cryopreservation of gametes or embryos.
